  "question": {
    "text": "&nbsp;If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo largeop=\"true\">&#931;</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&#8734;</mo></munderover><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>N</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math> is the set of all natural numbers, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></math> is"
